---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseStudyResult from "../../components/CaseStudyResult.astro";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="StubHub — Payments and Legacy Backend Work | Rashtan Soft"
  description="A case study of Gavrilo Mumovic's professional payment and backend work at Viagogo / StubHub."
  socialDescription="Professional experience improving payment and legacy backend systems in an established platform."
  eyebrow="Professional experience"
  caseTitle="StubHub — payments and legacy backend work"
  summary="At Viagogo / StubHub, I worked on backend and payment systems: payment-provider integrations, an automated payment method update platform and business logic moved from SQL Server into backend services."
  meta={[
    { label: "Company", value: "Viagogo / StubHub" },
    { label: "Role", value: "Senior Software Engineer" },
    { label: "Period", value: "September 2022–December 2023" }
  ]}
  factsHeading="Role context"
  facts={[
    { label: "Primary area", value: "Backend and payment systems" },
    { label: "Platform context", value: "A large legacy codebase" },
    { label: "Team support", value: "Mentored 3 junior developers" }
  ]}
>
  <h2>Insurance payments that were going unclaimed</h2>
  <p>The platform was entitled to insurance payments that it was not claiming. I found the unused payment insurance flow by reading the legacy code and documentation and asking colleagues how it was meant to work.</p>
  <p>I implemented the flow so those insurance payments could be claimed. Putting that existing entitlement into use contributed nearly $5M in additional revenue.</p>

  <CaseStudyResult
    label="Commercial contribution"
    value="Contributed nearly $5M in additional revenue through a payment insurance flow."
  />

  <h2>Payment-provider integrations and updates</h2>
  <p>I built payment-provider integrations using .NET Web API and gRPC. I also developed an automated payment method update platform using SQL Server queues and .NET Web API.</p>

  <h2>Moving business logic out of SQL Server</h2>
  <p>I moved business logic from legacy SQL Server code into backend services.</p>

  <h2>Supporting the team</h2>
  <p>After several senior engineers left the team, I mentored three junior developers alongside my payment and backend work.</p>

  <section class="case-technologies" aria-labelledby="stubhub-technologies">
    <h2 id="stubhub-technologies">Technologies</h2>
    <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Viagogo and StubHub technologies">
      <li>.NET Web API</li>
      <li>gRPC</li>
      <li>SQL Server</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

